Project9 dev bug log

fixed

- the authentication database accepted records with mismatched account identifiers
  verify record names and the expected uid for each database slot
  reject oversized and malformed account databases before hashing or saving

- password changes could write a record without validating the full destination
  require a shadow file with an aligned bounded size and the correct record slot

- tinyx compared authorization cookies with an early exit
  reject weak cookie lengths and compare every cookie byte before acceptance

- tinyx could sleep in poll before dispatching requests it had just buffered
  submit client requests before dispatch and wait for the next server deadline

- fragmented framebuffer damage could copy a large rectangle around small updates
  keep more damage rectangles and copy contiguous full width rows in one pass

- fvwm used a button event number where the drag loop needed a release mask
  stop coalescing motion events at the button release

- p9term repainted unchanged cells when repeated enter scrolled the terminal
  track the displayed cells and draw only changed runs

- the single height vbe console recopied unchanged rows when scrolling
  compare the text rows before copying their pixels to the framebuffer

- pty writes woke readers and poll waiters for each byte
  notify once per batch and before blocking on a full queue

- release builds could publish separate architecture disks and raw components
  ship one bios disk with both kernels and keep the installer payload inside it

- the boot menu mixed boot choices with loader controls and hid the default architecture
  label disk and live entries with their bitness and default to x86_64 when available

- top did not recognize the project9 console and could exit after one snapshot
  recognize the console terminal and enable interactive refresh on both kernels

- the base utilities under usr bin were built only for i386
  build and validate both native slices of top and vi for the shared release
  keep native libc file offsets and time records at the syscall widths

- top inherited a multi second refresh interval
  sample every half second by default and keep the user supplied delay

- a parallel release build could read an incomplete x11 sdk header
  publish each header after the copy is complete

- the host build advertised separate configuration and emulator targets
  build the bios release disk and sets with one release command
  boot the same raw image in qemu or from supported physical media

- ata flush could fail after a successful full disk test
  the driver used a fixed count of polls for completion
  slow host flushes could exhaust that count while the disk was busy
  wait against the kernel timer and keep reporting real io failures
  verify with a delayed flush and an offline ext2 check

- ehci usb storage worked in qemu but initially failed on the thinkpad
  the dma records omitted space for some extended address words
  give the queue head and transfer descriptor separate aligned storage
  with all high address words present and zero on this dma path
  the thinkpad sl510 subsequently enumerated two storage devices

- switching the build architecture could reuse shared output paths
  keep kernel objects user objects staged roots disks and release sets
  in their architecture profile
  verify by building both profiles from the same source tree

- the release checker rejected universal executables as invalid elf32
  validate both slices inside their own bounds and check each elf class
  keep the existing section and symbol table checks for both slices

- native shell and ed lacked a runtime for restoring a saved context
  save the x86_64 callee saved registers along with the stack and return pc
  use a native signal return stub with the stack aligned for calls
  verify shell syntax recovery ed error recovery and job control

- the kernel tests used i386 syscall entry and pointer width assumptions
  keep the stack probe on i386 and check wide pointer rejection on x86_64
  read the complete flags register on each abi and compare sbrk errors
  using a pointer sized sentinel

- the tinyx host and server exceeded the project9 user stack together
  allocate transport queues on the heap so the core can process requests
  without hitting the stack guard page

- tinyx passed its internal client capacity to project9 select
  cap the descriptor limit at the fd set size before polling

- the release check rejected ext2 executables above the old xv6 limit
  use a per slice limit that fits the ext2 release profile
  keep the legacy limit for images that still use the xv6 filesystem

- freetype reached the guard page while loading a truetype font
  give user programs a larger guarded stack at exec
  verify with the bundled font and p9font --check on both kernels

- sleep took ticks as its default unit and the apic timer used a fixed count
  sleep now takes seconds and preserves tick input through the t option
  calibrate the local apic timer against the pit on boot

- clear and the pager did not behave inside p9term
  clear through the terminal escape sequence and handle the pager form feed
  give the foreground pager its own cbreak state on each controlling pty
  open the matching pty for keyboard input when paging a pipe

- upstream xterm had no keyboard focus when started without a window manager
  focus the terminal when xinit starts it as the session client
  advertise input focus to the window manager and route keys to the vt widget
  verify by typing commands into a window away from the initial pointer

- xt could not parse floating point resources through project9 sscanf
  use strtod to read those resources on project9

- enter in xterm moved downward without returning to the first column
  translate line feeds on the pty slave when opost and onlcr are enabled
  apply the same output rule to echoed input and preserve raw line feeds

- tinyx rendered directly to mapped video memory
  render to normal memory and copy damaged rows after each server step
  reuse the sdk copy dispatch for long rows

open

- one ehci port on the thinkpad reported reset or companion routing
  while both attached storage devices were detected
  capture the controller and port state with the device connected
  distinguish a failed reset from a successful companion handoff
  then check the device on the companion controller where applicable

- usertests can stop at the large sbrk allocation on a 128 mib live guest
  the live root reserves about 32 mib and the test asks for 100 mib
  use at least 192 mib for the full live suite or boot a disk root
  a permanent test fix should size the large allocation using usable
  memory while retaining a separate check for allocation rollback

- disconnected usb disks consume minor slots until reboot
  reusing a slot today would let an old open handle refer to a new disk
  give usb handles a device generation before allowing slot reuse

- exiting fvwm with two terminal clients can fault the x86_64 console shell
  qemu reproduced it after opening xterm from the fvwm menu and leaving x
  the fault was in the native shell variable list lookup
  reproduce with the sse only qemu cpu and trace writes to the shell list
  standalone xterm sessions returned to the console in the same build
